diff --git a/tools/README.md b/tools/README.md
index aa45c2f5..cea07300 100644
--- a/tools/README.md
+++ b/tools/README.md
@@ -197,6 +197,15 @@ that identity after its byte copy (or residency reuse), avoiding another scan
 of Chip RAM. The same identity permits borrowing the eleven host-prepared
 health glyph records without runtime directory lookup or planar extraction.
 A stale artwork object cannot link to a different payload identity.
+The same generator composes the fixed gameplay HUD backdrop (both margins,
+both borders and ammo-bar artwork) into two complete 384-by-284 planar images.
+Gameplay entry publishes these ordinary-memory words once, before mutable
+health/text/ammo updates. It clears only the game ring: every HUD word,
+including padding, is overwritten by the prepared backdrop. No extra Chip
+buffer is allocated. `REFERENCE_HUD_BACKDROP=1` retains the layered initial
+renderer and its HUD clear; the profiling script clears this selector when
+restoring the normal executable. The host pixel test compares both complete
+planes, not only the visible border pixels.
 Generic packs still use exact byte admission and runtime glyph preparation.
 `make -C amiga verify-health-link`
 in the Amiga environment verifies both matching and mismatched object pairs.
diff --git a/tools/generate-amiga-health-art.cpp b/tools/generate-amiga-health-art.cpp
